 "key_note": "Vigenère on the tabula recta, key MANCHESTERBLUFF running across the cipher words and advancing by plaintext length (targets/johnston1863/check.py). Tiles marked uncertain are the clerk's slips: the key letter C applied as E twice, and an N left in clear; the tile shows the letter of the 1863 'Translation of Cypher'. The last E of INVADE and one S of TENNESSEE were not written, so their key letters are passed over. Only 31 cipher letters exist, fewer than the usual 40.",
